64
00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:30.400
Your turn. Say: Flavorful.

65
00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:34.292
Flavorful.

66
00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:39.053
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:39.917 --> 00:03:42.021
Visal, can you cook a healthy dish?

68
00:03:43.117 --> 00:03:46.570
Yes! Chicken and vegetable soup.

69
00:03:47.683 --> 00:03:48.766
How do you make it?

70
00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:53.730
First, I marinate the chicken with garlic and pepper.

71
00:03:54.817 --> 00:03:55.411
Then?

72
00:03:56.517 --> 00:04:02.559
Then I simmer it with fresh ingredients. Finally, I garnish it with herbs and serve it.

73
00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.525
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:06.383 --> 00:04:09.823
Grammar focus: Sequencing (first, then, finally).

75
00:04:10.123 --> 00:04:11.321
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:13.378
First, marinate the meat.

77
00:04:14.283 --> 00:04:15.517
Then simmer it.

78
00:04:16.417 --> 00:04:18.114
Finally, garnish and serve.

79
00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:23.960
Put a comma after 'First' and 'Finally'. Use the imperative (base verb) for each step.

80
00:04:24.717 --> 00:04:28.902
Be careful! Don't say: Finally garnish and serve it first.

81
00:04:30.867 --> 00:04:33.574
Say: Finally, garnish and serve.

82
00:04:33.874 --> 00:04:36.513
Use 'Finally' for the last step, with a comma.

83
00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.150
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:40.933 --> 00:04:42.178
My Healthy Soup.

85
00:04:42.478 --> 00:04:45.035
Cooking at home helps me keep a balanced diet.

86
00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:48.695
First, I marinate the chicken in garlic and pepper.

87
00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:52.466
Then I simmer it with fresh, wholesome ingredients.

88
00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:56.244
Finally, I garnish it with basil to make it flavorful.

89
00:04:57.233 --> 00:05:00.673
Meal prep on Sunday helps me control my portion size.

90
00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:06.152
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:07.017 --> 00:05:08.540
blank, marinate the meat.

92
00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:12.575
A, First. B, Finally. C, Then finally.

93
00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:17.889
The answer is A: First.

94
00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.769
To cook slowly just below boiling is to blank.

95
00:05:22.069 --> 00:05:25.537
A, simmer. B, garnish. C, marinate.

96
00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.169
The answer is A: simmer.

97
00:05:32.317 --> 00:05:34.339
Healthy and good for you is blank.

98
00:05:34.639 --> 00:05:38.571
A, wholesome. B, flavorful. C, substituted.

99
00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:43.924
The answer is A: wholesome.

100
00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:48.436
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:49.283 --> 00:05:51.898
Describe a healthy recipe you know how to cook.

102
00:06:00.683 --> 00:06:02.300
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:11.956
I can cook fried rice with vegetables. First, I cook the egg. Then I add rice and vegetables. Finally, I garnish it with green onion.

104
00:06:12.256 --> 00:06:13.989
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:14.883 --> 00:06:20.310
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and sequencing (first, then, finally).

106
00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:25.329
Today's value is healthy eating. Eat fruit and vegetables to grow strong.

107
00:06:25.629 --> 00:06:28.282
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

108
00:06:28.582 --> 00:06:31.304
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

